From e8c967c02f32bb3503240b7437acd8f4113d0810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:21:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-28: the HTML style and attributes of the source,
 editable in the property grid (0.28.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The panel's HTML section lists what the SOURCE's start tag writes -- the style
declarations as written (not the browser's longhands: border:1px outset was
a dozen border-* rows) and the attributes as written (the page's JS strips
titles at run time) -- and they can be changed like WPF changes the XAML:
- double-click a value -> an input; Enter or leaving it commits (a changed
  value only), empty = remove, Esc cancels;
- "＋ 樣式名稱 / 值" adds a declaration (z-index, border ...);
- attributes: title, class, placeholder, tabindex, alt, data-*, aria-*;
  never the id (the page's JS finds the control by it) nor an on* handler;
- checked twice (extension and probe): a CSS name of lowercase letters and
  '-', a value without ; { } < > \ -- so nothing can leave its declaration;
  a locked component's position properties are refused.
- The probe writes it (setStyleRaw / setAttrRaw) and reports the edit; one
  Ctrl+Z. htmledit.attrsOf.

Tests: lib 121 (attrsOf: spbSave's class/id/title/style, bare and unquoted
ones), probe (z-index / title written, onclick never, removal), smoke 94
(the data: left 54px, id not editable, title editable; only the clean style
and the text attribute reach the probe), panels (double-click left -> 54px
-> Enter posts 60px; id not editable; the new-style row; title), real VS
Code 96 (z-index:5 in spbSave's source, the panel shows it, one undo) -- all
pass; NO-SAVES, MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
